---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="People — VIOT Research" description="Principal Investigator and research context.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="kicker">People</p>
    <h1>Principal Investigator</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div>
        <div style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1;border-radius:12px;background:var(--panel-2);border:1px solid var(--edge);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
          <span style="font-family:var(--font-serif);font-size:4rem;color:var(--navy);opacity:0.15;">SP</span>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.4rem;">Shantanu Pawar</h3>
        <p class="text-small" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">
          Dept. of Mechanical Engineering<br>
          PVG's College of Engineering, Technology and Management<br>
          Pune, Maharashtra, India
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" style="font-size:1rem;">
        <p>Sole author of the Virtual Ion-Optics Testbed (VIOT) research program. The work focuses on the multiscale assessment of carbon-nanomaterial accelerator-grid coatings for charge-exchange (CEX) erosion mitigation in the NASA NSTAR ion thruster.</p>
        <p>The research combines:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Plasma Physics:</strong> GPU PIC-MCC (Particle-in-Cell with Monte Carlo Collisions) simulations.</li>
          <li><strong>Atomistic Modeling:</strong> LAMMPS AIREBO crystalline Molecular Dynamics for ion-surface interactions.</li>
          <li><strong>Computational Engineering:</strong> Custom 3D Poisson solvers and DSMC (Direct Simulation Monte Carlo) pipelines.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <h2>Research Timeline</h2>
    <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>2024</h3>
        <p class="text-small">Phase I: MATLAB prototype. Phase II: VIOT-2 GPU PIC-MCC prototype. 15 defects discovered.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>2025</h3>
        <p class="text-small">Phase III: VIOT-3 axisymmetric production framework. 70/70 tests pass. Phase IV: VIOT-4 3D + DSMC + MD framework initiated.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>2026</h3>
        <p class="text-small">Phase V: Consolidated manuscript (35 pp). VIOT-4 core complete. Campaign results finalized.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <h2>Documentation Record</h2>
    <p class="prose" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Every number, parameter, algorithm, file, result, and known defect of the VIOT program — sufficient to reproduce the work from scratch or audit any claim in the manuscript.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Contents</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="mono">01_Project_Overview.md</td><td>Research question, hypotheses H1–H4, scope, timeline, current status</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">02_Data_Campaign_Results.md</td><td>All 36 campaign simulations, per-seed raw erosion, LEF derivation</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">03_Data_EBS_Analysis.md</td><td>10-seed electron-backstreaming ensemble, barrier physics, LEF_EBS</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">04_Data_Yield_Tables.md</td><td>All 7 sputter-yield tables, RustBCA + LAMMPS generation parameters</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">05_Data_Neutral_DSMC.md</td><td>Analytic view factor vs DSMC benchmark, the 44.4% deviation</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">06_Physics_and_Math.md</td><td>Every governing equation, constant, and derivation used</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">07_Codebase_VIOT3.md</td><td>Axisymmetric framework: file-by-file, every module, every API</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">08_Codebase_VIOT4.md</td><td>3D framework: file-by-file, DSMC, MD pipeline, 3D Poisson</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">09_Verification_and_Tests.md</td><td>All 70 tests + 2 VIOT-4 tests, what each asserts, all results</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">10_Results_Summary.md</td><td>Every headline result with its provenance chain</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">11_Empirical_Reference_Data.md</td><td>NSTAR ELT data, published sputter yields, grid geometries</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">12_Framework_Comparison.md</td><td>VIOT vs. existing tools (Orbitrap, ONERA, etc.)</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">13–17</td><td>Manuscript history, known issues, reproducibility, references, inventory</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
